stateDiagram-v2
%% Source connection states
%%
%% The four states the `sources` capability requires, and every move between them.
%% Board for the `source-lifecycle` change, requirement 3 (Connection state).
%%
%% Read from:
%%   apps/android/core/model/.../Source.kt      SourceConnectionState, ReconnectBackoff
%%   apps/android/core/model/.../SourceProbe.kt  stateForStatus, stateForFailure, isRemote
%%
%% A local folder never enters this machine: SourceProbe.isRemote answers false for
%% LOCAL_FOLDER, because whether a folder is readable is a question for the filesystem
%% rather than one to back off from.
    [*] --> Connecting: source added, or app launched

    Connecting --> Connected: HTTP 200-299
    Connecting --> Unauthorized: HTTP 401 or 403
    Connecting --> Unreachable: any other status, or no answer at all

    Connected --> Unreachable: request fails
    Connected --> Unauthorized: credential refused

    Unreachable --> Connecting: backoff elapsed
    Unreachable --> Connecting: network regained, or foreground

    Unauthorized --> Connecting: RECONNECT

    note right of Connecting
        State is never persisted. It describes a network,
        and a state read back from disk is a claim about
        the past — so something re-probes after a launch.
    end note

    note right of Connected
        canFetch = true. The only state that can serve a
        title which is not already downloaded.
    end note

    note right of Unreachable
        Neutral indicator, never a red error badge:
        offline is a normal state, not a failure.
        Downloads stay readable; titles that are not
        downloaded are dimmed and not openable.

        Backoff starts at 5 s and doubles to a 5 min cap.
        The retry on network-regained or foreground fires
        immediately, once.

        404 lands here on purpose rather than in a fifth
        "gone" state: a catalogue that has moved is, to a
        reader, a catalogue that is not answering, and a
        reconnect may still fix it.
    end note

    note right of Unauthorized
        needsUserAction = true — the only state the reader
        has to act on.

        RECONNECT re-opens the sheet the source was added
        through, address filled in and secret blank. What
        comes back carries the same identifier, so
        SourceRegistry.replacing puts it back with its
        position, its downloads and the reader's own name
        for it intact. "Remove and re-add" loses all three.
    end note
